#: ../../tools/pdbe_sifts_tools.rst:94 e2638ac7f6394ac4a12c2cb1f990d809
msgid ""
"**Description**: Map PDB entry chains to UniProt protein accessions using"
" PDBe SIFTS cross-referencing. For a given PDB structure, returns which "
"UniProt proteins are present, which chains correspond to each protein, "
"and the residue-level mapping between PDB and UniProt numbering. "
"Essential for understanding multi-chain structures and identifying "
"proteins in crystal/EM structures. Example: PDB 1tup maps chain A/B/C to "
"P04637 (TP53) residues 94-312."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/pdbe_sifts_tools.rst:98 6da5c18f49854fdbb4c37ba238433aee
msgid ""
"``pdb_id`` (string) (required) PDB entry ID (4-character code). Examples:"
" '1tup' (p53-DNA complex), '1m17' (EGFR kinase), '3pxe' (BRCA1 BRCT), "
"'4hhb' (hemoglobin)."
msgstr ""

